  "route": "original",
  "notes": "Backlog game, all-AAA pass: picked from RAWG's most-added list for its year across all genres (docs/PLAN.md section 2, genre filter widened 2026-10-23). RAWG's first result is the expected entry \"the-walking-dead\" (id 23027). RAWG lists the five episodes as additions, plus \"The Walking Dead: 400 Days\" and \"The Walking Dead Collection - The Telltale Series\". Steam app 207610 (\"The Walking Dead\" in the store list; its schema is named \"ValveTestApp207610\", a placeholder) was used. None of the 48 Steam achievements is hidden. The episode names come from the RAWG description and match the Episode 1 to 3 achievements. The six achievements with API names \"WalkingDead106\" name the chapters of Vince, Wyatt, Russell, Bonnie and Shel and an Epilogue, and two more (\"Two out of Three\", \"Reunited\") share that prefix; they are probably 400 Days, but the data does not say so, so the chapter is named after the five characters. StrategyWiki redirects \"The Walking Dead: Season One\" to \"The Walking Dead\", at completion stage 1: Episode 1: A New Day (about 7,600 characters) and Episode 2: Starved for Help (about 7,800) are written, with the Table of Contents; Episodes 3 to 5, Walkthrough, Gameplay, Characters and Achievements and trophies are linked but not written. Two of five episodes was not judged a good enough share, so it was not used. walkingdead.fandom.com has no page under \"The Walking Dead: Season One\", \"The Walking Dead: Season 1\", \"The Walking Dead (Video Game)\", \"The Walking Dead (Telltale)\" or \"The Walking Dead: The Game\"; its API search found \"Season 1 (Telltale)\", with about 165 linked articles, which is used; names only were looked at, nothing copied."
}
